tem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://takuapa101.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Wat Senanuch Rangsan (Wat Mai), Takua Pa\", \"item\": \"https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-sena/\"}]}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"TouristAttraction\", \"name\": \"Wat Senanuch Rangsan (Wat Mai)\", \"url\": \"https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-sena/\", \"image\": \"https://takuapa101.com/assets/wat-sena.webp\", \"description\": \"The ordination hall’s architecture includes Chinese elements and reflects Thai-Chinese culture.\", \"address\": {\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\", \"streetAddress\": \"Old Market, Takua Pa Subdistrict\", \"addressLocality\": \"Takua Pa\", \"addressRegion\": \"Phang Nga\", \"addressCountry\": \"TH\"}, \"geo\": {\"@type\": \"GeoCoordinates\", \"latitude\": 8.8302299579, \"longitude\": 98.3624509671}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the history of this place?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The temple was founded in 1847 (พ.ศ. 2390) by Phraya Senanuchit (Nuch Na Nakhon), ruler of Takua Pa. The temple register gives the founding year as 1847 (พ.ศ. 2390) and identifies it as a Maha Nikaya public temple.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is there to see?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"See the large ordination hall, which the ONEP database says was influenced by Chinese architecture. A tourism source says there is a museum displaying antiques, including a wooden pulpit bearing the initials จปร. Check on-site whether it is open to visitors. See the temple grounds registered as an ancient monument in 1996 (พ.ศ. 2539).\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How do municipal documents describe this place?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The ordination hall’s architecture includes Chinese elements and reflects Thai-Chinese culture.\"}}]}]",
